# Funds Manager AI workflow

Follow this loop for every delivery. Do not skip steps unless the user explicitly says so.

## 1. Ticket (GitHub) — **first step when starting work**

- Work from a **GitHub issue** on [Project #5](https://github.com/users/kgz/projects/5/views/1).
- **Immediately** move cards to **In progress**:

```bash
./bin/board-status.sh in-progress <issue-num>
```

- When closing: `./bin/board-status.sh done <issue-numbers...>`
- PR must reference them with `Closes #N`.

## 2. New branch (from `main`)

```bash
git checkout main && git pull origin main
git checkout -b feature/<issue>-<short-slug>
```

## 3. Spec (OpenSpec — on `main` first)

- On **`main`**: `/opsx:propose` → `openspec/changes/<change-name>/`
- Then checkout the delivery branch and commit spec artifacts there.

## 4. Explore / apply (on delivery branch)

- Optional: `/opsx:explore`
- **`/opsx:apply`** on `feature/<n>-<slug>` only — implement `tasks.md`, check off `- [x]` as you go.

## 5. Test & quality

- `cargo test` in `app/`, `database/`, and affected `crates/`
- `cd frontend && pnpm run build` before PR when UI changes
- Manual QA for affected routes before PR

## 6. Pull request + link ticket

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base main --head feature/<n>-<slug> \
  --title "..." --body "## Summary\n...\n\nCloses #<issue>"
```

## 7. Archive spec (before or right after merge)

- `openspec archive <change-name> -y` (syncs specs and moves to archive)
- Or manually sync `openspec/specs/` and move to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`

## 8. Merge

- Merge PR after review (and CI if present).

## 9. Ticket → Done

- `./bin/board-status.sh done <issue-numbers...>`
- `gh issue close <n> --repo kgz/Funds-Manager`

